.rem Every feature of the language on one page. Panel 0: ink and
.rem placement. Panel 1: fills. Panel 2: the repertoire. Panel 3:
.rem links and the odd cases. The page starts in panel 0 without
.rem saying so. The title bar is an alias, used on every panel.
.def bar TITLE
.fg white
.bg blue
.fill 0
.at 0
$TITLE
.fg
.bg
.enddef
.bar FEATURES · ΟΛΑ · 1/4
.at 2
.fg red
RED at column 0: the code is in
.fg green
GREEN the tail of the row, and
.fg yellow
YELLOW text keeps its column.
.fg blue
BLUE
.fg magenta
MAGENTA
.fg cyan
CYAN
.fg white
WHITE
.fg default
.at 10
plain then
.fg cyan
+ cyan then
.fg default
+ plain again.
.fg cyan
LABEL
.fg default
.col 8
value on the label's row
.at 12
 leading spaces position the run
   and paint nothing, so this
     staircase keeps its ground.
.at 16
.fg yellow
    Four spaces in: the code
.fg default
    takes the blank before the
text, and column 0 returns.
.at 20 10
.at 20 6
.at 20 2
One-shot .at: this run is at
column 2 and the next is back at
column 0.
.fg white
.bg blue
.fill 27
.at 27 2
INK · ΜΕΛΑΝΙ
.bar FEATURES · ΟΛΑ · 2/4
.at 2
fill R           one full row:
.bg red
.fill 3
.fg default
.bg default
.at 4
fill R C         from a column:
.bg green
.fill 5 10
.bg default
.at 6
fill R C ROWS    a banner:
.bg yellow
.fill 7 4 3
.fg default
.bg default
.at 10
fill R C ROWS COLS    a box:
.bg magenta
.fill 11 8 3 12
.bg default
.at 14
Text over a fill keeps its
ground: only the foreground is
paid for, in the gap before it.
.bg cyan
.fill 18 0 1 30
.fg blue
.at 18 2
BLUE ON CYAN
.fg white
+  WHITE
.fg default
.bg default
.at 20
A default fill clears anything.
.bg red
.fill 21
.bg default
.fill 21 6 1 20
.at 23
Two attributes, two gaps:
.fg white
.bg blue
+  BAR
.fg default
.bg default
.fill 27
.fg white
.bg blue
.fill 27
.at 27 2
FILLS · ΓΕΜΙΣΜΑΤΑ
